-- title:
--   Evaluation at a place equals pull-back along an O-section
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\neq 0$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, and $\rho\colon R_q\to A$ a ring map whose composite with $A\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the structure map; assume the residue field of $A$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $q$. Let $\mathfrak P$ be a `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`, so in particular it supplies a curve model $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{Meta}$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(N_0q))=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with an isomorphism $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{eeta}$ onto the generic-fibre base change of `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q`. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal generated by $q$, equipped with a ring isomorphism $e_O$ onto $A\cap F$ where $F$ is the fixed field of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$, a map $\rho_O\colon R_q\to O$ compatible with $R_q\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ through $O\cong A\cap F\subset F\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and a map $\mathrm{to}\kappa\colon O\to$ `ResidueField A` given by reduction of that embedding. Write $\mathfrak X_O$ for the pullback of `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\rho_O$, assumed integral, let $x$ be a point of $\mathfrak X_O$, and let $\varphi$ be a ring map from the function field of $\mathfrak X_O$ to `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)` subject to two normalisations: on germs at $x$ of global sections pulled back from $O$ it is the embedding $O\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ above (hypothesis on constants), and on the functions of the chart algebra `IgusaScheme.chartAlgFin (N₀ * q) q`, transported through the open immersion `IgusaScheme.ιFin (N₀ * q) q` and $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$ to the function field, it is the coefficientwise embedding of their $q$-expansions into Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; the preimage of the chart is assumed non-empty. Let $V$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $t\colon\operatorname{Spec} O\to\mathfrak X_O$ be a section of $\mathrm{pullback.snd}$ whose base change along $O\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$, followed by $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$, is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point attached to $V$ by $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$ pushed forward by $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{eeta}$ and $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$. Assume $t$ sends the closed point of $O$ to $x$ and that $x$ lies in the preimage of the chart. Then for every germ $s$ of the structure sheaf at $t(\text{closed point})$, the image $\varphi(s)$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar (N₀ * q)` of $s$, transported to the function field, lies in the valuation subring of $V$, and $V.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of it — the element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ mapping to its residue class — is the image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of `Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo t s`, the pull-back of $s$ to $O$ along $t$.
--
--   This is the level-$N_0q$ form of the statement that the value at a place $V$ of a function arising from a germ on the integral model equals the specialisation of that germ along the $O$-section through $V$, the evaluation-matching step linking the divisor-theoretic language of places on $\overline{\mathbb Q}(X_0(N_0q))$ with the scheme-theoretic model over $O$. It is used in the analysis of chart presentations at nodes, in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_nodeCoordinates_and_forall_mem_support_iff_chainPos_of_chartPresentation`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_nodeCoordinates_and_forall_mem_support_iff_chainPos_of_chartPresentation).
